# SPECTRA canvases — open them; do not rely on a click

On this Windows workspace, a markdown link with `C:\...` **does not open**. Backslashes break the link. The user has asked repeatedly to pop canvases beside the chat.

Whenever you create, update, or mention a `.canvas.tsx`:

1. **Call `open_resource`** (cursor-app-control) with
   `file:///C:/Users/User/.cursor/projects/c-SPECTRA-CompressionAgent/canvases/<file>.canvas.tsx`
   Do not wait for the user to click.
2. In chat, link with **forward slashes** (POSIX), never a `C:\` path:

```
[Gilad brief](/Users/User/.cursor/projects/c-SPECTRA-CompressionAgent/canvases/spectra-gilad-brief.canvas.tsx)
```

Canvases live only in that `canvases/` directory (Cursor-managed). Do not put `.canvas.tsx` in the git repo.
